---
import '@fontsource-variable/source-serif-4';
import '@fontsource-variable/inter';
import '../styles/global.css';
import CookieNotice from '../components/CookieNotice.astro';

const title = 'Privacy · MindLynx';
const updated = '27 July 2026';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-GB">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content="How MindLynx handles the details you send us." />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#07110f" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://mindlynx.ai/privacy" />
    <script is:inline src="/tachyon-emit.js" defer></script>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="site-header is-scrolled">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="MindLynx home">
        <img class="brand-mark" src="/images/brand-mark.png" alt="" width="31" height="31" />
        MindLynx
      </a>
      <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Site">
        <a class="nav-cta" href="/#talk">Talk to us</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="legal">
      <div class="shell">
        <p class="section-label">Privacy</p>
        <h1>What we do with your details.</h1>
        <p class="legal-lead">
          Short version: we use what you send us to reply to you, and for the Albion waitlist if
          you ask for it. We don't sell it, share it, or add you to anything you didn't choose.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          Three things. First, what you type into the contact form or into a form Vera (our site
          companion) shows you in chat: your name, your email address, what you're writing about,
          and your message. Second, anonymous visit measurement through our own first-party
          analytics (Tachyon): which pages load, what gets clicked, where a visit came from, your
          device type and how fast the page loaded. Third, if you choose to talk to Vera, the
          conversation itself: your messages (and your audio, if you turn voice on) are sent to
          Google Gemini to generate her replies, for the duration of the conversation only. We do
          not store transcripts, and the chat resets when you leave the page. No advertising
          trackers, no third-party analytics, no cross-site anything.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          We set one cookie: <code>_tch_vid</code>, a random identifier that lets us recognise a
          returning browser for up to a year. A companion session identifier
          (<code>_tch_sid</code>) lives only until you close the tab. Both are first-party, are
          never shared, and contain nothing about who you are. Your browser's cookie controls
          remove them at any time. Preferences you choose on the site (like dismissing the cookie
          notice) are stored locally in your browser and never leave it.
        </p>

        <h2>Why we hold it</h2>
        <p>
          To answer you. That's our legitimate interest in responding to someone who has
          deliberately contacted us, and the same basis covers our anonymous visit measurement.
          The Helix and Albion announcement lists are different: we only add you when you tick the
          consent box on the form, we record when you ticked it, and you can withdraw at any time
          by unsubscribing or emailing us. Talking to Vera is entirely optional, and everything on
          the site works without her.
        </p>

        <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
        <p>
          Our email is delivered by <a href="https://resend.com/legal/dpa" rel="noopener">Resend</a>,
          which processes messages on our behalf and hosts the announcement lists. The site is
          served by Render, our visit measurement runs on our own Tachyon service, and Vera's
          replies are generated by Google Gemini, which receives the conversation only while you
          are chatting. All act as processors under our instructions. Nobody else receives your
          details, and we never sell them.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Correspondence stays in our inbox while it's useful, and we clear it out when it isn't,
          within two years at the latest. Waitlist entries stay until the product launches or until
          you unsubscribe, whichever comes first.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under UK GDPR you can ask us for a copy of what we hold, ask us to correct or delete it,
          object to how we're using it, or withdraw consent for the waitlist. Email
          <a href="mailto:hello@mindlynx.ai">hello@mindlynx.ai</a> and we'll action it. No forms,
          no friction. If we get it wrong, you can complain to the
          <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">Information Commissioner's Office</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          MindLynx Ltd, registered in England and Wales, company number 17226845, London,
          United Kingdom. Data protection questions go to
          <a href="mailto:hello@mindlynx.ai">hello@mindlynx.ai</a>.
        </p>

        <p class="legal-meta">Last updated {updated}.</p>
        <a class="partner-link" href="/">Back to MindLynx <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div class="shell">
        <span>MindLynx Ltd · Company No. 17226845 · London</span>
        <span>Building in Britain · Building in the open</span>
      </div>
    </footer>

    <CookieNotice />
  </body>
</html>
